{"nodes": [{"id": "incoming_build183_parts_rebuild_build183_rebuild_build183", "label": "REBUILD-BUILD183 Procedure", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "incoming/BUILD183-PARTS/REBUILD-BUILD183.md", "source_location": "L1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A 5.9 MB bundle cannot be created through the Drive connector, which takes content inline only - so the bundle is never uploaded, its derivation is, with an md5 on every input and every step."}, {"id": "incoming_build183_parts_rebuild_build183_build183", "label": "BUILD183 compendia bundle", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "incoming/BUILD183-PARTS/REBUILD-BUILD183.md", "source_location": "step 5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "5,920,198 B, md5 d215c184aee08b884d8748fb6d79c0cb, 66,990 lines, 353 members."}, {"id": "incoming_build183_parts_rebuild_build183_close_py", "label": "close.py (the guarded close)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "incoming/BUILD183-PARTS/REBUILD-BUILD183.md", "source_location": "step 4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Carries its own reverse guard: stripping the appended text must recover the old bundle's md5. Any mismatch stops the chat with a report; nothing is patched into agreement."}, {"id": "incoming_build183_parts_rebuild_build183_part_size_cap", "label": "The 5 KB Part Cap", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "incoming/BUILD183-PARTS/REBUILD-BUILD183.md", "source_location": "L31-L39", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "base64Content with disableConversionToGoogleType removes the TRANSPORT failure mode but not the TRANSCRIPTION one: at ~8-10 KB of base64 this chat produced two wrong uploads in four attempts, one truncated to 205 B against 6,023, both caught by the read-back byte count. Keeping every part near 5 KB has not yet